// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  CONTRACT C — a third foreign-language term. One β step; it is the one the desk will accept.
//
//  Run me with the RhoCalc interpreter:
//    target/debug/rhocalc demos/flt-assay-desk/contract-c.rho
//
//  THE TERM — feed the constant combinator to the identity
//  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//        I = lam x. x             the IDENTITY combinator (= λ.0)
//        K = lam a. lam b. a      the CONSTANT combinator (= λ.λ.1)
//
//  This file is the redex
//        I K
//  which β-reduces in a SINGLE step, because the identity just hands back what it was given:
//        I K   ⟶β   K
//
//  Note what this means for the assay desk: Contract C ARRIVES as `(lam x. x, lam a. lam b. a)`,
//  which is not the constant combinator — it only BECOMES the constant combinator after the
//  machine reduces it. The desk's predicate is over the RESULT, so the reduction has to have
//  actually happened for C to be accepted.
//
//  EXPECT
//  ──────
//        normal form on @"OUT"  =  ⟦λ.λ.1⟧                the constant combinator K
//        ^fired ledger          =  ["Beta"]               1 in-Rho rewrite firing
//        ^drive-err / ^drive-fuel empty                   ⟹ it terminated by QUIESCENCE
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

lam`(lam x. x, lam a. lam b. a)`
